      },
      {
        &quot;id&quot;: &quot;ad_d70d7ecd-3d25-4ed3-9e50-91c7dc0f1b32&quot;,
        &quot;projectId&quot;: &quot;cmrd6tbvr000ai0wcli5yek70&quot;,
        &quot;label&quot;: &quot;Egyptianizing Uraei&quot;,
        &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pair of uraei flanking the solar disk. The snakes are represented in the characteristic Egyptian manner as rearing cobras with expanded hoods, symmetrically arranged on either side of the disk. This iconographic scheme is strongly Egyptianizing and recalls royal and divine symbols widely used in ancient Egyptian art, where the uraeus represented protection, sovereignty, and divine authority. The association of the solar disk with paired uraei is a well-established motif in Egyptian religious iconography and reflects the close cultural interactions between the Punic and Egyptian worlds.&quot;,
        &quot;class&quot;: &quot;ocra-voc:uraeus&quot;,
        &quot;content&quot;: {},
        &quot;visibilityType&quot;: &quot;scene&quot;,
        &quot;visibilityId&quot;: &quot;scene_0a317693-dad3-4866-8d38-a6556224370b&quot;,
